## Scope

After technical validation works, apply the private golden retrieval gate and
the published resource budgets to decide which curated entries are exposed and
whether the default changes. Compatibility crowd counts are supporting
operability evidence only.

## Exit criteria

- Every proposed shipped entry passes local compatibility, the golden retrieval
  gate and resource limits on its supported shapes.
- Licences, artifact sizes and runtime support are disclosed beside the entry.
- The decision and its negative controls are recorded in DECISIONS.md.
- If evidence does not justify a change, MiniLM remains the default explicitly.
